Privacy Policy for TwoDone

**Effective Date:** March 16, 2026

1. Introduction
Welcome to **TwoDone** ("we," "our," or "us"). We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information when you use the TwoDone mobile application (the "App").

2. Data Collection and Usage
**TwoDone does NOT collect, transmit, or store your personal data on any external servers.** 
All data generated by your use of the App, including your tasks, statistics, experience points (XP), username, and usage history, is stored **locally on your device**. 

We do not require you to create an account, nor do we ask for personal identifiable information (PII) such as an email address or phone number.

3. Local Storage
The App uses local device storage (such as SQLite and Shared Preferences) to function properly. This includes:
* Saving your task lists and categories.
* Tracking your completion history and streaks.
* Storing your Premium subscription status and app settings (e.g., Dark Mode).
If you uninstall the App or clear its data, all of this locally stored information will be permanently deleted unless you have created a manual backup using your device's operating system features.

4. Device Permissions
To provide certain features, the App may request the following permissions:
* **Storage / Photos / Media:** Required only when you use the "Generate Annual Report" or "Share Stats" features. The App takes a local screenshot of your statistics and saves it to your device's gallery so you can share it. We do not access your personal photo library for any other purpose, and we never upload your photos to our servers.

5. Health and Fitness Data
Due to the nature of task and habit tracking, you may choose to enter information related to your health or physical fitness (e.g., workout routines, medication reminders, or diet tracking). 
* **Collection and Access:** The App does not integrate with device health sensors or APIs (like Google Fit or Apple Health). The only explicitly health-related data collected is the text you manually input as your tasks.
* **Usage:** This data is used solely to provide the core functionality of the App (tracking your tasks and progress).
* **Storage and Sharing:** Any health or fitness-related information you enter is stored **locally on your device**. It is **not** transmitted to our servers, **not** shared with third parties, and **not** used for advertising or tracking purposes.

6. Third-Party Services and Analytics
TwoDone is a standalone application. We currently do not integrate any third-party analytics or advertising SDKs (such as Google Analytics or AdMob) that track your behavior across other apps or websites. 
*Note: The app distributes through platforms like Google Play Store and Apple App Store, which may collect basic crash reports and download statistics automatically as part of their standard terms of service. You can control these settings directly through your device's OS settings.*

7. Premium Subscriptions (In-App Purchases)
If we implement third-party payment gateways (such as RevenueCat or Google Play Billing) for Premium features in the future, your payment transactions will be processed directly and securely by those providers (e.g., Google or Apple). We do not collect, process, or store your credit card information.

8. Children's Privacy
Our App does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13. Since no data is transmitted to our servers, we inherently do not collect data from children.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Thus, you are advised to review this page periodically for any changes. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

10. Contact Us
If you have any questions or suggestions about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us at: o1e3studio@gmail.com
